    <desc>Open tabs in containers, and keep new tabs in the container you work in.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Toolbox and Distrobox containers</title>

<p>If you use <app>Toolbox</app> or <app>Distrobox</app>, the main menu has
  <gui style="menuitem">New Tab in Container</gui>, which opens a tab with a
  shell in one of your containers. The containers are found with
  <cmd>podman</cmd>.</p>

  <p>New tabs and panes that you open from a terminal in a container start in
  the same container. For that, the shell in the container has to report it,
  which it does in <app>Toolbox</app>, or the terminal has to be started in it
  from <app>Pano Terminal</app>. To turn this off:</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and select <gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui>.</p></item>
<item><p>In the <gui>Behavior</gui> group, turn off <gui>Keep New Tabs in the Same Container</gui>.</p></item>
</steps>

